d Taxes Found to Be Slightly Progressive\"</a>. <i>Tax Foundation</i>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Tax+Foundation&amp;rft.atitle=Contrary+to+Popular+Belief%2C+Value-Added+Taxes+Found+to+Be+Slightly+Progressive&amp;rft.date=2020-08-13&amp;rft.aulast=Enache&amp;rft.aufirst=Cristina&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Ftaxfoundation.org%2Fvalue-added-tax-vat-progressive%2F&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AValue-added+tax\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-4\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-4\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Chia-Tern Huey Min (October 2004) <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20071129192831/http://adb.org/Documents/Events/2004/Fourteenth-Tax-Conference/text-chia.pdf\">GST in Singapore: Policy Rationale, Implementation Strategy &amp; Technical Design</a>, Singapore Ministry of Finance.</span>\n</li>\n</ol></div></div>"}}}